  "project_description": "Collapsiblock makes all individual Drupal blocks collapsible. To show/hide the content of a block just click on its title.\n\n When configured: the last state of blocks is saved in a cookie for each user.\n\n This module is intended for site-builders who are new to Drupal with relatively simple needs. We try to accomodate feature requests and options but will balance those with the need for a simple UI.\n\n Blocks open and close with a slide animation, powered by the lightweight\n\n alexmcarthur/slide-element library (bundled in) - no jQuery required.\n\n For menu blocks you can keep the active trail open, so a block containing a\n\n link to the current page stays expanded. Uncheck that setting if you'd rather\n\n it behaved like any other block.\n\n \n Example sites ( ? ):\n\n \n https://arst.dk/kort \n \n \n Credits: \n\n \n QED42 sponsored development and port from 7.x-1.x to 8.x-1.x",
